  "title": "Theme",
  "definition": "The [term:semantic-role] assigned to a participant whose location or state is described, or that is moved without undergoing a change of state. Theme is often distinguished from [term:patient] by the absence of a change-of-state implication. In stative predicates the [term:subject] is typically a theme.",
